+## Source and candidate relationship
+
+A real HEAD alone is insufficient. The verifier checks current source blobs against its Git tree and rejects changed, deleted and untracked source. No uncommitted version-plan transformation is currently supported. A workflow that intentionally changes versions without a commit must provide a separately reviewed, reproducible transformation interface before M3 can pass. This session has no exact active model identity hook and cannot create a commit. It also has no authorization to publish, push or tag.
+
+M1 accepts stable/shared scope (12 packages, 14 minimum/current consumer rows). M2 accepts exact RC19 preview/shared scope (6 packages, one exact preview consumer). M3 requires the complete 13-package, 15-row candidate in addition to both milestones. Global fingerprints and global manifest file hashes are diagnostic/M3 bindings; they cannot substitute for scoped source/build/artifact receipts.
+
+## Native execution evidence
+
+The verifier uses the existing comprehensive `tools/check-coverage.mjs` gate for 54 × 7 stable coverage and its actual native public API, story/request, behavior, accessibility and review checks. Tracking rows, staged descriptors and empty suites never award coverage.
+
+T13 matrices live at `test-results/t13/{compatibility,ssr}-runs/<run>/results.json`. The newest relevant run is selected exactly once. An unfinished, missing, stale or failed new run never falls back to an older pass. Missing/stale/unperformed evidence is blocked; a proven current failed execution is failed.
+
+Recorded source-before/source-after and tested-output snapshots are compared with freshly regenerated complete canonical inventories, including path sets. Added files or outputs invalidate old evidence. An all-framework snapshot may be projected only by removing foreign adapter and fixture roots; every remaining shared, root, test and selected-framework input must exactly match the fresh scoped inventory. Thus preview-only source changes do not overwrite stable evidence. Actual command names, nonempty original log hashes and all nine browser/timezone outcomes with the producer's exact required checks are validated. Explicit skipped/unexecuted/nonzero contradictions are rejected.
+
+T14 artifact and consumer receipts must bind each scope separately to current source, build and selected artifact bytes. Consumer acceptance requires the canonical producer's reviewed validator for original command/log receipts, exact runtime/compiler resolutions, lock/config bytes, installed candidate bytes and actual SSR/browser outcomes. Legacy `checks: passed` strings and arbitrary nonempty logs are insufficient.
+
+## Pending producer and human interfaces
+
+The earlier generic `acceptance-evidence.json` row protocol is withdrawn. Hash-bound flags, arbitrary observations and arbitrary or empty logs cannot establish native execution, independent review or authentic human acceptance. There is currently no implemented trusted producer-specific validator for indexed patterns, six-pilot preview behavior, CI execution acceptance, independent review, manual sessions or documentation review. These gates stay blocked even if someone supplies apparently complete indexed JSON. Actual producer interfaces must be integrated and reviewed before they can pass.
+
+`docs/reviews/manual-gates.json` remains an explicit human-review blocker. A present VoiceOver application, screenshots, automated DOM checks, synthetic signal/media or CSS zoom cannot supply screen-reader speech review, original-media/sign-language equivalence, real browser zoom, forced-colors or focus-visibility acceptance.
+
